; TLS models in Linux PIC code (ABI.md "Dynamic linking"), from getTLSModel:
; a PIE uses local exec for a dso_local variable and initial exec for the
; others (`leapc %gottprel(v)`, an invariant GOT load, TP + offset or the
; r + r index of the access); a shared library uses general dynamic for
; every variable (local dynamic too), `leapc r0, %tlsgd(v)` and an ordinary
; call of __tls_get_addr (R12 = the address), unless the tls_model attribute
; asks for a faster model.  A dso_local variable is named by its local
; alias there (`.Lloc$local`, STT_TLS).  Code that is not PIC (STATIC) is
; local exec throughout, as in tls.ll.

@loc = dso_local thread_local global i32 1, align 4
@ext = external thread_local global i32, align 4
@arr = external thread_local global [16 x i64], align 8
@ld = internal thread_local(localdynamic) global i64 0, align 8
@ie = external thread_local(initialexec) global i32, align 4

